IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-payment`

-- ind-c-tests-procedure.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of ss.42-44 and 48-50 (gazette pp. 193-195).
-- Scenario ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.  Periods: Interpretation Law s.10(a) (N days from a day,
-- that day not counted); s.10(c) applied to the deadlines and windows here (fleet ruling 4), with rest days chosen
-- by the test.  Every expected date is a literal computed by hand (and its weekday checked with Python).

§ `ind-c: ss 42 to 44 and 48 to 50`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

GIVEN days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`rest on` days MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS days

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of intention`
`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` d MEANS
    `Notice of intention` WITH
        `delivered on` IS d
        `in writing` IS TRUE
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
        `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
        `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
        `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS TRUE
        `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS TRUE
        `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS TRUE
        `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS FALSE

-- A notice that omits (b)(4), the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and its rate.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of intention`
`ind-c a notice without (b)(4) delivered on` d MEANS
    `Notice of intention` WITH
        `delivered on` IS d
        `in writing` IS TRUE
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
        `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
        `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
        `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS TRUE
        `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS TRUE
        `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS FALSE
        `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS FALSE

-- A notice that omits (b)(1), the act and its date.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of intention`
`ind-c a notice without (b)(1) delivered on` d MEANS
    `Notice of intention` WITH
        `delivered on` IS d
        `in writing` IS TRUE
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS FALSE
        `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
        `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
        `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS TRUE
        `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS TRUE
        `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS TRUE
        `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS FALSE

§§ `D1-D2: s 42(b), what the notice of intention states`

#ASSERT `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` (`ind-c a notice without (b)(4) delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` (`ind-c a notice without (b)(1) delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)))

§§ `D3-D6: s 43, thirty days from the delivery of the notice`

-- D3: notice delivered Monday 2027-03-01: last day Wednesday 2027-03-31; representations that day are in time.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31
#ASSERT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2027 3 31) `is within the period for representations of` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days`
-- D4: 2027-04-01 is late.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 43 — the day` (YMD 2027 4 1) `is within the period for representations of` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days`)
-- D5: notice delivered Thursday 2027-02-04: nominal last day Saturday 2027-03-06; that day a rest day: Sunday 2027-03-07.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 2 4)) NOTHING (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 3 6))) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 7
#ASSERT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2027 3 7) `is within the period for representations of` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 2 4)) NOTHING (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 3 6)))
-- The alternative without s.10(c): 2027-03-06.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice, without s 10(c)` (YMD 2027 2 4) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 6
-- A rest day inside the period does not move its end.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 3 13))) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31
-- D6: an extension to 2027-04-15 granted for special reasons that were recorded: the period ends 2027-04-15.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) (JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` WITH `the period now ends on` IS YMD 2027 4 15, `special reasons were recorded` IS TRUE)) `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 15
-- D6: the same extension with no reasons recorded is not the extension s.43 allows: the 30 days stand.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) (JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` WITH `the period now ends on` IS YMD 2027 4 15, `special reasons were recorded` IS FALSE)) `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31

§§ `D7, D10: s 44(d), the notice treated as a payment demand, and s 48 after it`

-- D7: notice 2027-03-01, no representations: treated as a demand delivered on 2027-03-31, the last day of the s.43 period.
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44(d) — the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING `no rest days` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 31)
-- D10: then 30 days to pay: 2027-04-30.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days`) `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 30
-- D7 with s.10(c): notice 2027-02-04, 2027-03-06 a rest day: the s.43 period ends 2027-03-07, the demand is treated as
-- delivered then, and payment is due by 2027-04-06.
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 2 4)) NOTHING (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 3 6))) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 7
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2027 3 7) (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 3 6))) EQUALS YMD 2027 4 6

§§ `D8-D9, D11-D12: s 48, thirty days to pay, and s 49, a late payment`

-- D8: demand delivered Monday 2027-05-10: last day Wednesday 2027-06-09; paid that day: on time.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2027 5 10) `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 6 9
#ASSERT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 9) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 5 10) `with` `no rest days`
-- D9: paid 2027-06-10: late.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 10) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 5 10) `with` `no rest days`)
-- D11: demand delivered 2027-02-04: nominal last day Saturday 2027-03-06, a rest day: 2027-03-07.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2027 2 4) (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 3 6))) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 7
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand, without s 10(c)` (YMD 2027 2 4) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 6
-- D12: s.49, late means after the last day.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 6 9) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 6 9))
#ASSERT `s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 6 10) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 6 9)
-- Paid on time: the sanction alone, whatever interest would have been.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20000 `when the payment is late:` FALSE `with shekel interest` NOTHING `and arrears fees` NOTHING EQUALS 20000
-- Paid late, with the Interest and Linkage Law's amounts supplied (an input): the sanction plus both.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` (JUST 150) `and arrears fees` (JUST 50) EQUALS 20200
-- Paid late with no amounts supplied: the Law's rates are outside the sources, so no number.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` NOTHING `and arrears fees` NOTHING

§§ `D13-D16: s 50, instalments`

-- D13: at the violator's request, 12 monthly payments: within what the Law allows.
#ASSERT `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 12 TRUE
-- D14: 13: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` TRUE 13 TRUE)
-- D15: no request by the violator: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` FALSE 6 TRUE)
-- D16: a payment missed: the decision is void and the balance is due at once.
#ASSERT `s 50(b) — the decision on instalments is treated as void and the balance falls due at once` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(b) — the decision on instalments is treated as void and the balance falls due at once` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 50(b) — the balance of the debt that falls due at once on a sanction of` 12000 `of which` 4000 `has been paid` EQUALS 8000

§§ `X9: s 44(d), the deemed delivery, both readings checked`

-- On the last day of the s.43 period (taken, 2027-03-31), or the day after it (2027-04-01).
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered, counting from the day after the period ends` (`ind-c a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 1
